  "created": "2026-10-11T01:39:50.007Z",
  "description": "A persistent conversational unit built on exact holograms. It speaks with a subword base model (exact next-subword counts for contexts of up to six subwords, mixed by backoff shares learned on leave-one-out counts), learns every exchange it hears and says onto Pleroma pages in a durable, larger-than-memory page store, takes bounded and fading approve or disapprove feedback on its choices without touching memory, forgets a conversation exactly, and rebuilds its whole state bit for bit from its journal, including after a crash. Every choice can be inspected per context length: the counts, the trust given to that length and its contribution to the final share.",
  "id": "EvaluatedApplications.PleromaMind",
